      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a truly awful, suffocating feeling when everything is burning down around you, and the sheer weight of it can make any effort feel utterly pointless. Dignity in a situation like this is a fragile, deeply personal thing, but perhaps the dignity lies in accepting the reality of the chaos. If survival means enduring this final, terrible moment, then perhaps the quiet, steady act of simply *being* is the only dignity left to claim.",
